DESIGN DECISIONS
- Evidence EMBEDDED, not linked. Signed URLs live 60 minutes; a pack of
  links is broken by the time an accountant opens the email. Files are
  fetched during generation and written into evidence/ with a
  manifest.csv mapping each to the schedule line it supports.
- Client-side generation, matching the existing tax report. Keeps large
  binaries off the server and lets progress be shown per document.
- PARTIAL FAILURE IS REPORTED, NEVER FATAL. A document that cannot be
  fetched is named on the PDF cover and marked "NOT INCLUDED" in the
  manifest; the pack still builds. Same for unconfirmed loan statements
  and capital works items lacking a completion date - both surface as
  omissions rather than quietly shrinking a total.
- The questionnaire states what is NOT tracked. A silently omitted section
  reads as "nothing to declare", the one reading that could make a return
  wrong. Every untracked question is emitted with a null answer and an
  explicit status.
- Cost base is stated at 100%, NOT apportioned, and the PDF says why: a
  disposal is calculated per owner at the time. Everything else in the
  pack is the apportioned share.
- A QS Div 43 figure supersedes the computed register, because the
  surveyor also values original construction the owner never paid for.

DEFECT FOUND BY RUNNING AGAINST REAL DATA
The register was wired with a pre-filter that dropped capital works items
having no completion date. That defeated div43RegisterForFy's own
itemsMissingStartDate reporting - the omission warning could never fire,
and the pack would have shown zero Division 43 with no explanation.
Corrected to pass every capital works item and let the register report
the gaps. On the user's real property this changes silence into
"10 capital works item(s) have no completion date, so no Division 43
deduction is claimed for them". Unit tests did not catch this; only
running it against restored production data did.

Related note: the local DB was restored from prod via db:sync, which
predates migration 057, so capital_works_start_date is null there. The
backfill will populate it when 057 is applied to production.

